1. Passwordless SSH Failed
Error
Permission denied (publickey)

Cause
SSH public key was not present in the managed node's authorized_keys file.

Resolution
Generated an SSH key pair on the Ansible Master.
Copied the public key to the managed nodes.
Verified SSH connectivity using:
ssh ec2-user@<private-ip>


2. Host Key Verification Failed
Error
Host key verification failed

Cause
A stale or mismatched host key existed in ~/.ssh/known_hosts.

Resolution
Removed the old host key and accepted the new fingerprint.
ssh-keygen -R <private-ip>

Verified using:
ssh -v ec2-user@<private-ip>


3. Inventory Not Working
Error
No hosts matched

Cause
Incorrect inventory configuration or group name mismatch.

Resolution
Validated the inventory:
ansible-inventory -i inventory --list


4. YAML Indentation Error
Error
did not find expected '-' indicator

Cause
Incorrect indentation in the playbook.

Resolution
Used two-space indentation consistently.
Verified syntax before execution.
ansible-playbook --syntax-check site.yml


5. Handler Not Running
Issue
Apache did not restart after playbook execution.

Cause
No changes were detected in the template task, so notify was not triggered.

Resolution
Modified the template, reran the playbook, and confirmed the handler executed only when changes occurred.

6. Role Not Found
Error
The role 'users' was not found

Cause
The role was referenced in site.yml but had not been created.

Resolution
Created the role:
ansible-galaxy init roles/users


7. Template Module Error
Issue
The template could not be found.

Cause
Incorrect path used inside the role.

Incorrect
src: ../templates/index.html.j2

Correct
src: index.html.j2
Within a role, Ansible automatically searches the role's templates/ directory.
